            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for injection, then the French for waiting room."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: guérir",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "guérir — \"to heal, to cure; to get better\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ma grand-mère a guéri de sa grippe en une semaine. My grandmother got over her flu in a week."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Guérir de — to recover from. A regular -ir verb: nous guérissons."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "guérir comes from Frankish warjan \"to protect, to defend\" (EtymDB), a Germanic word; the sense moved from \"protect\" to \"heal\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
